COMMAND NAME: mppaddmirrors.sh

Adds mirror segments to a Bizgres MPP system that was initially 
configured without mirroring.


*****************************************************
SYNOPSIS
*****************************************************

mppaddmirrors.sh -d <master_data_directory> [-p <port_base>] 
[-l <logfile_directory>]

mppaddmirrors.sh [-? | -v]


*****************************************************
DESCRIPTION
*****************************************************

The mppaddmirrors.sh script configures mirror segment instances 
for an existing Bizgres MPP system that was initially configured 
with primary segment instances only. The script will shut down your 
Bizgres MPP system while it creates the mirrors, and then restart it 
with mirroring enabled.

MIRROR DATA DIRECTORIES

The script will prompt you for the data storage location(s) where it 
will create the mirror segment data directories. The script will create 
a unique data directory for each mirror segment instance in this location 
using a predefined naming convention. 

There must be the same number of data directories declared for mirror 
segment 
instances as for primary segment instances. It is OK to specify the same 
directory name multiple times if you want your mirror data directories 
created in the same location, or you can enter a different data location 
for each mirror. Enter the absolute path. For example:

Enter mirror segment instance directory 1 of 2 > /mpp_mirror
Enter mirror segment instance directory 2 of 2 > /mpp_mirror

OR

Enter mirror segment instance directory 1 of 2 > /mppdata/dbfast3
Enter mirror segment instance directory 2 of 2 > /mppdata/dbfast4

You must make sure that the user who runs mppaddmirrors.sh (for example, 
the bgadmin user) has permissions to write to these directories. You may 
want to create these directories on the segment hosts and chown them to 
the appropriate user before running mppaddmirrors.sh.


*****************************************************
OPTIONS
*****************************************************

-d <master_data_directory>

Required. The data directory of the MPP master instance.

-p port_base

This specifies the base port number on which mirror segment instances 
will be started on a segment host. If a host has multiple mirror segment 
instances, the base port number will be incremented by one for each 
additional mirror segment instance started on that host. If not provided, 
the mirror segment ports will be calculated based on the available ports 
in the range of 1000 - 65500.

-l <logfile_directory>

The directory to write the log file. Defaults to ~/mppAdminLogs.

-?

Displays the online help.

-v

Displays the version, status, last updated date, and check sum of this script.


*****************************************************
EXAMPLES
*****************************************************

Add mirroring to an existing Bizgres MPP system:

mppaddmirrors.sh -d /mpp_master_data -p 20000


